\description{
Download a PRIDE project's files, all of them or a selection, into a directory and report the paths written.

Files are streamed to a temporary name and moved into place only once complete, so an
interrupted download never leaves a truncated file behind.
}
\details{
Prefer \code{\link{pride_download_files}} when you can. \code{category} and \code{extensions} can only express
what they were built to express; "under 5 MB", "the three newest", or "everything except the
MGF" cannot be said in that vocabulary at all - and can all be said with \code{[}.
}
\value{
A character vector of the paths where the files now are.
}
